 of the AI Boom's Dark Side</h3>
            <p>The rapid adoption of generative AI and autonomous agents has =
significantly expanded the digital attack surface for enterprises, driving a =
surge in demand for advanced cybersecurity solutions. Bad actors are leveragi=
ng AI to automate and scale attacks.</p>
            <p>Traditional security systems are proving inadequate against AI=
-driven threats, forcing companies to rethink how they protect identities, en=
dpoints, and cloud infrastructure. Consequently, the global cybersecurity mar=
ket is projected to reach $663 billion by 2033.</p>
            <p class=3D"trend-summary">For financial investors, cybersecurity=
 stocks represent a highly resilient and strategic play on the AI boom. As cy=
ber threats grow more sophisticated, enterprise spending on security infrastr=
ucture will remain a non-discretionary priority.</p>
